  "hindi": "हे व्रत धारण करनेवाले, हे वेगवान् आदित्यो, अपराध को मुझसे दूर कर दो, जैसे गुप्त रूप से प्रसव करनेवाली स्त्री करती है। हे वरुण, हे मित्र, हे देवो, भलाई को जाननेवाला मैं सुननेवाले तुम सबको सहायता के लिए पुकारता हूँ।",
  "english": "O Ādityas, firm in ordinance and vigorous, put the offence far from me, like a woman who gives birth in secret. Knowing what is good, I call on you who hear, O Varuṇa, O Mitra, O gods, for help.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "'dhṛtavratā' is the bahuvrīhi 'having firm ordinances'. 'iṣirāḥ' rendered 'vigorous' (also 'swift, fresh'). 'rahasūr iva āgaḥ': the simile is obscure to the drafter (rahasū, a woman who bears in secret); only the literal words are given and the point of comparison is not explained. 'vidvān' printed with a nasal sign (vidvā~): Vedic sandhi before avase. 'śṛṇvataḥ vaḥ' taken as accusative 'you who hear'. 'bhadrasya vidvān' taken as 'knowing the good'.",
  "confidence": "low"
 },
