  "hindi": "हे देवो, तुम पूर्वविचार हो, तुम बल हो; तुम द्वेषों को दूर रखो। हे अभिभूत करनेवालो, क्षमाशील बनो, और आज तथा आगे भी हम पर कृपा करो।",
  "english": "You, O gods, are forethought; you are strength; keep the hatreds far away. O overpowering ones, be forbearing, and today and afterwards be gracious to us.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "'abhikṣattāraḥ' is unclear to the drafter; rendered 'overpowering ones' (a derivation from abhi-√kṣad or abhi-kṣatṛ); it may be a nominative qualifying yūyam. 'pramatiḥ' rendered 'forethought'. 'sanutaḥ' taken as 'far away, aside'; 'yuyota' as impv. of √yu 'keep off'. The two verbs 'kṣamadhvam' and 'mṛḻayata' are imperatives.",
  "confidence": "low"
